  "description": {
    "text": "The fifth POP Series set, 17 cards Pokémon Organized Play gave out in two-card packs at its leagues and tournaments from March to September 2007. It finished bringing into English the Japanese promos English players had been missing, the Gold Star Espeon and Umbreon among them, and it is the most sought-after POP set today.\n\nEvery card in the packs is non-holo, the Gold Stars too. Holo copies came later in shop products: Mew δ and Pikachu in DP Value Pack 1 (Wal-Mart and Target, September 2007), and Ho-Oh, Lugia, Pelipper δ and Zangoose δ in DP Gift Packs (Target and Toys \"R\" Us, October 2007). The holo Mew δ and Pikachu are known with their back printed upside down."
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "The POP Series 5 symbol, and a number out of 17"
  },
